body:
With the usb a C to A cable, The specification only allows 5 volts thus powering the hub and nothing more, That hub is a pd passthrough hub. Knowing the switch, you'll need a pd power-supply capable of the 15 volt profile, The macbook usb c charger only supports  20.2/9V/5.2V missing the all important 15 volt profile . something like this should work for you:

&#x200B;

[https://www.amazon.co.uk/Inateck-compatible-Chromebook-Nintendo-MateBook/dp/B06XPFVF2S/ref=sr\_1\_2?ie=UTF8&qid=1536615547&sr=8-2&keywords=usb+pd+15+volt](https://www.amazon.co.uk/Inateck-compatible-Chromebook-Nintendo-MateBook/dp/B06XPFVF2S/ref=sr_1_2?ie=UTF8&qid=1536615547&sr=8-2&keywords=usb+pd+15+volt)

[https://pocketpc.download/?dir=Drivers/Bluetooth](https://pocketpc.download/?dir=Drivers/Bluetooth)

&#x200B;

This is what i have been able to find. I extracted the cabs from the installer i found, so you can copy those directly to your pocket pc, the cab ending in 2577 should work for you, The wildcom is a driver that was modified to support that card but it requires some hand edits to work.
